sequenceDiagram
    actor User as CLI User
    participant picocli as picocli CommandLine
    participant SC as SetupCommand
    participant STS as AWS STS
    participant IAM as AWS IAM
    participant S3 as AWS S3
    participant CFSvc as CloudFormationService
    participant CF as AWS CloudFormation
    participant FS as Local Filesystem

    Note over User,FS: baas admin deployment setup -- needs the elevated BaasCliDeployerPolicy.<br/>Deploys the CORE stack only. cf-template-ci.yaml is deployed by hand.
    User->>picocli: baas [--deployment D] admin deployment setup [--region] [--deployer-aws-profile]<br/>[--use-existing-vpc --vpc-id --subnet-id --sg-id]
    picocli->>SC: parse and bind options into fields
    Note over SC: validate federation and networking options before anything is loaded --<br/>a partial federation set, or --vpc-id/--subnet-id/--sg-id without<br/>--use-existing-vpc (or the flag without all three) -> exit 2 (U34)
    SC->>FS: ConfigService.load()
    FS-->>SC: loadForSetup() -- deployments/D.yaml (or a new one named D), else the only one,<br/>else empty: the name is derived below. Two or more and no D: refused. D validated first, before any AWS call
    Note over SC: apply --region / --deployer-aws-profile over config defaults
    SC->>STS: sts.getCallerIdentity()
    STS-->>SC: account id
    Note over SC: prefix = D, the only configured one, else "baas-" + accountId<br/>stackName = bucketName = prefix<br/>tableName = prefix + "-results" (DeploymentNames)<br/>Nothing about the CALLER reaches the name -- a second<br/>deployment exists only because its name was typed.
    SC->>S3: headBucket(bucketName) -- bucketRegion?
    Note over SC,S3: global: a wrong-region request answers 301/400 with x-amz-bucket-region,<br/>and 404 = no bucket. Needs only s3:ListBucket on the prefix bucket
    alt bucket in ANOTHER region
        SC-->>User: the deployment lives there -- setup --region <it>, exit 1, no delete advice (U23)
    end
    Note over SC: BEFORE the preflight: a deployer's grants name one region, so elsewhere<br/>the preflight would print a policy inviting a second deployment
    SC->>IAM: SimulatePrincipalPolicy(critical actions) -- opportunistic preflight
    alt denied
        SC-->>User: stderr names the denied actions, STDOUT holds the rendered deployer<br/>policy (setup > policy.json hands it over) -- exit 1, nothing created
    end
    SC->>FS: load /templates/cf-template-core.yaml from the classpath
    FS-->>SC: template body

    SC->>CF: describeStacks(stackName) -- exists?
    alt stack exists (update)
        Note over SC: networking params sent only if this invocation named them,<br/>and refused if they differ from the deployed values.<br/>Federation params carried forward unless named or revoked.
        Note over SC: image parameters: only those the deployed stack lacks.<br/>Base, parent and extension are carried forward, so a plain<br/>setup never reverts an image or drops an extension
        SC->>CFSvc: updateStackParameters(stack, template, changed params)
        alt status ROLLBACK_COMPLETE
            CFSvc-->>User: refuse -- delete it first with<br/>baas admin deployment teardown --deployment X --yes
        else updatable
            CFSvc->>CF: updateStack(named params + UsePreviousValue for the rest)
            alt nothing changed
                CF-->>CFSvc: "No updates are to be performed" -- reported as already up to date
            else changes applied
                CFSvc->>CF: waiter.waitUntilStackUpdateComplete()
            end
        end
    else stack absent (create)
        Note over SC: every image parameter is planned (parent resolved by<br/>DescribeImages in this region), never left at a template placeholder
        SC->>CFSvc: createStack(stack, template, explicit params incl. federation or empty)
        CFSvc->>CF: createStack(CAPABILITY_IAM, CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM)
        CFSvc->>CF: waiter.waitUntilStackCreateComplete()
    end

    SC->>CF: describeStacks() -- OperatorRoleArn output, to print only
    SC->>FS: ConfigService.save() -- deployments/<prefix>.yaml: prefix, aws.deployerProfile, resolved aws.region
    SC->>FS: write ~/.baas/runner-image-extension.yaml (beside deployments/, never in it), only if absent
    Note over SC,FS: nothing derivable or resolvable is stored

    alt created
        SC-->>User: BaasCliOperatorRole created -- nobody can assume it yet.<br/>1. grant sts:AssumeRole + add a ~/.aws/config profile (see infra/README.md)<br/>2. baas config set --operator-aws-profile NAME<br/>Next: baas admin image build (~15 min)
    else updated
        SC-->>User: "Deployment <prefix> is deployed. Operator role: <arn>"
    end

    SC-->>User: exit 0
